# •••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••
# 🔐 MEDIAMTX — INTERNAL AUTH USERS (EXAMPLE) 🔐
# •••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••

# Generated form of this file is ./config/users.env — produce it with
# ../mediamtx-users.sh rather than editing by hand. This example exists to
# show the shape, and to be readable when the real file is absent.
#
# Two things must both be true for any of this to take effect:
#   1. config/mediamtx.yml has `authMethod: internal` and
#      `authInternalUsers: []` uncommented.
#   2. compose.yaml lists this file under env_file (it already does).
#
# Why the empty list in mediamtx.yml matters: MediaMTX merges these variables
# into the existing list field by field rather than replacing it, so leftover
# permissions from the built-in entry at the same index survive. Tested
# 2026-08-13: a user written here as publish+read came back from the API as
# publish+read+playback, inherited from built-in entry 0.
#
# Why every value is single-quoted: Compose interpolates unquoted env_file
# values, and an argon2 hash starts with `$argon2id`, which reads as a variable
# reference. Single quotes make Compose treat the value literally.
#
# Indices are contiguous from 0. Actions: publish, read, playback, api,
# metrics, pprof. An empty PATH means every path; empty IPS means any source.

# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
#                                   🔑 USER 0 — PUBLISHES THE CAMERA, READS ANY PATH, FROM ANYWHERE
# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_USER='instructor'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_PASS='argon2:$argon2id$v=19$m=4096,t=3,p=1$c2FsdEl0V2l0aFNhbHQ$replace-with-a-real-hash'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_IPS=''
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_PERMISSIONS_0_ACTION='publish'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_PERMISSIONS_0_PATH=''
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_PERMISSIONS_1_ACTION='read'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_0_PERMISSIONS_1_PATH=''

# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
#                                  👀 USER 1 — VIEWS THE `cam` PATH ONLY, FROM THE CLASSROOM SUBNET
# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_USER='student'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_PASS='argon2:$argon2id$v=19$m=4096,t=3,p=1$YW5vdGhlcnNhbHQ$replace-with-a-real-hash'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_IPS='192.168.1.0/24'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_PERMISSIONS_0_ACTION='read'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_PERMISSIONS_0_PATH='cam'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_PERMISSIONS_1_ACTION='playback'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_1_PERMISSIONS_1_PATH='cam'

# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
#                            🧰 MANAGED TAIL ENTRY — KEEPS API, METRICS AND PPROF REACHABLE LOCALLY
# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
# mediamtx-users.sh always writes this last. Without it, `authInternalUsers: []`
# leaves the API with no permitted user at all and `docker compose logs` is the
# only way to see anything.
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_2_USER='any'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_2_PASS=''
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_2_IPS='127.0.0.1,::1'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_2_PERMISSIONS_0_ACTION='api'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_2_PERMISSIONS_1_ACTION='metrics'
MTX_AUTHINTERNALUSERS_2_PERMISSIONS_2_ACTION='pprof'

# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
